entityDescription:
SME4SPACE is a Panel of Space SMEs Associations of the ESA Member States and ESA cooperating States. SME4SPACE was founded in 2007 and officially launched on 19 June 2007 at the International Paris Air Show, Le Bourget. On that day ESA General Director J. J. Dordain signed a Memorandum of Agreement formalising cooperation between ESA and SME4SPACE. This Agreement was recently renewed at the ESA Industry Space Days 2016 and in 2019.
The aim of SME4SPACE is to voice Space SMEs' viewpoint in a coordinated way and to facilitate the access of SMEs to space activities in general and to ESA adn EU programmes in particular.
More in detail the organisation pursues the following not for profit purposes:
- defining and defending common positions, representing the SMEs towards public authorities i.e. the European Space Agency, the European Commission and its related agencies;
- organising seminars and information sessions;
- organising a network of SMEs in order to increase the possibilities to cooperate;
- carrying out research projects, participating at National, European and International calls in space and related activities. 

SME4SPACE is incorporated as a not for profit organisation under the Belgian Law in Leuven, VAT N. BE0837709024.

Nowadays SME4SPACE gathers 20 Space SME Associations/Clusters, and 26 Individual Company Members. Full and updated list of SME4SPACE Members is available at the following page: https://www.sme4space.org/sme4space-members
